module gunbc.rung_drop_amendment.v2_test_family_reds_measured_outside_the_gate

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.rung_drop_amendment { RungDropAmendment }

// The v2.test. family is inside required_gate_bankruptcy's population (every witness outside the
// roster), and its return is that row's restoration trigger, so the measured reds are an AMENDMENT to
// it and not a second drop behind the same trigger (deep-ferret-305, on gunbc#12860).
data v2_test_family_reds_measured_outside_the_gate: RungDropAmendment = RungDropAmendment {
  drop_identity: "required_gate_bankruptcy" as NonEmptyStr,

  amended: "2026-10-01",

  later_event: "the srv1 probe of the withdrawn v2.test. family (neat-boar-16, scratch commit eff2d73b14 = main c95f906 plus the family, artifacts on branch artifact/v2-gate-probe) measured what this row's population holds for that family: 841 v2.test.* modules declaring 5,030 test fns at c29acd041e1 have no required route; with the family restored, 4,265 were planned, 4,192 passed, 17 reached no verdict (route gaps already rostered by v2.workflow.floor_route_gap), and 44 were red on main with no lane observing them. Preparation dominated, about 3,569 modules resolved and 3,096 s wall against about 101 s of claim evaluation, the shape of this row's 2026-09-19 nominal-roster cut, so the family stays out until the trigger below. One module, v2.test.claim.cargo_build_run_argv_witness, did not typecheck on main and refused the whole floor in strict preparation when the family was restored; gunbc#12860 repaired it" as NonEmptyStr,

  bearing: "of the 44 measured red identities, those still red are named here with their owners, and each leaves this amendment's list when its fix lands, so restoring the family does not inherit them as silent reds. Owner deep-ferret-305 (floor lane), fixed by work item adhoc-e6c8990b-ccf: v2.test.name_resolve.test_code_reference_wall.supplied_root_is_what_normalize_emits_holds (returned false). The two rust_variant_construct_emit identities that work item named left this list when proud-wren-900 grounded unit-variant True on the binding-ref literal ladder (dag_binding_type_variant_true stays a coproduct arm, never a bool keyword), stopped treating BindingRef match as the int-bool octet channel, and retargeted complement/meet/join goldens and emit_host allocators onto dag_token_kw_true/false; emit_host_variant_construct_equals_eval left when its eval stub read ConstructTagEdge instead of a named Holds child the construct node does not carry. Owner calm-fox-43 (grammar lane), measured red in a SEPARATE measurement from the srv1 probe: gunbc run --claim-run on main eb60ee176d0 on 2026-10-01 (remote 48GB runner), identical on main's grammar and on gunbc#12920, so not caused by that change; cause not yet derived: v2.test.execution.emit_ingest_grammar_relation_round_trip.same_grammar_parse_ingest_bridge_holds (returned false); v2.test.execution.dag_add_emit_round_trip.dag_add_domain_coerce_accepts_holds (returned false); v2.test.execution.dag_add_emit_round_trip.dag_add_domain_translate_accepts_holds (returned false). None is an expected-red row: that roster asserts the identity executes, and these do not while the family is outside the gate" as NonEmptyStr,
}
